  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Samuel",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 30,
    "summary": "The Amalekites spoil Ziklag and the borders of Judah—David smites Amalek and regains and divides the spoil.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when David and his men were come to Ziklag on the third day, that the Amalekites had invaded the south, and Ziklag, and smitten Ziklag, and burned it with fire;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:1",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And had taken the women captives, that were therein: they slew not any, either great or small, but carried them away, and went on their way.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:2",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "So David and his men came to the city, and, behold, it was burned with fire; and their wives, and their sons, and their daughters, were taken captives.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:3",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Then David and the people that were with him lifted up their voice and wept, until they had no more power to weep.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:4",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And David’s two wives were taken captives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "1 Sam. 25:43; Jacob 2:24."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Sam. 25:43; Jacob 2:24.",
            "prettyString": "1 Samuel 25:43; Jacob 2:24",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1samuel",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 43,
                        "end": 43
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jacob",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 2,
                    "end": 2,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 24,
                        "end": 24
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:5",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And David was greatly distressed; for the people spake of stoning him, because the soul of all the people was grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters: but David encouraged himself in the Lord his God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 175,
            "end": 185,
            "text": "Ps. 56:3 (3–4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:6",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said to Abiathar the priest, Ahimelech’s son, I pray thee, bring me hither the ephod. And Abiathar brought thither the ephod to David.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:7",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And David inquired at the Lord, saying, Shall I pursue after this troop? shall I overtake them? And he answered him, Pursue: for thou shalt surely overtake them, and without fail recover all.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 156,
            "end": 161
          },
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 191
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:8",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "So David went, he and the six hundred men that were with him, and came to the brook Besor, where those that were left behind stayed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:9",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "But David pursued, he and four hundred men: for two hundred abode behind, which were so faint that they could not go over the brook Besor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:10",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And they found an Egyptian in the field, and brought him to David, and gave him bread, and he did eat; and they made him drink water;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:11",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And they gave him a piece of a cake of figs, and two clusters of raisins: and when he had eaten, his spirit came again to him: for he had eaten no bread, nor drunk any water, three days and three nights.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 164,
            "end": 167
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:12",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And David said unto him, To whom belongest thou? and whence art thou? And he said, I am a young man of Egypt, servant to an Amalekite; and my master left me, because three days agone I fell sick.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 42
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Samuel 30:13",
        "book": "1 Samuel",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "We made an invasion upon the south of the Cherethites, and upon the coast which belongeth to Judah, and upon the south of Caleb; and we burned Ziklag with fire.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 1:38."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 73
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Kgs. 1:38.",
            "prettyString": "1 Kings 1:38",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1kings",
